{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-10510022-e64b-4cd2-8932-e3645a852e0b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-86b5512d2e3f3511","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-x96818bq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store (branch A)\n\n> **Conditional branch epic — outcome A of the provisioning go/no-go decision.** Selected\n> only if the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled\n> operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5. If a different outcome is selected, this epic does\n> not exist.\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the preferred provisioning outcome: PostgreSQL lifecycle management for\nthe Gen AI Studio default vector store implemented in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\nprovided by the dashboard operator modularization, following the model-registry-operator's\nestablished auto-provisioning pattern. When a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG capabilities\nis configured, the operator provisions a dedicated PostgreSQL instance (with pgvector) in the\nplayground's namespace, and the remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration consumes\nthe provisioned connection string — giving users a default vector store that works\nout-of-the-box with no manual setup.\n\nThe ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic;\nthat is why the RHOAI-controlled operator layer is a hard prerequisite for this branch.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL self-provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer following the\n  model-registry-operator pattern: per-namespace Deployment, Service and credential Secret\n  created when a playground with RAG is configured, consumed via a connection string.\n- Use the existing Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector out of the\n  box — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding work.\n- Pin the database image for disconnected installs through the existing operator image\n  reference mechanism (the PostgreSQL 16 related-image environment variable already present\n  in the platform operator's CSV).\n- Apply resource requests/limits to the provisioned PostgreSQL instance starting from the\n  model-registry-operator's values, adjusted by the benchmark-derived sizing recommendation.\n- Scope the instance per namespace (per-namespace isolation is the selected scoping model).\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC\n  becomes available (RHOAI 3.6+), the configuration consumes the shared connection string\n  instead of self-provisioning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Configuring a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG causes a PostgreSQL instance (pgvector\n  included) to be provisioned in the playground's namespace, with no manual user setup\n  steps.\n- The provisioned instance's credentials are delivered via a Secret and consumed by the\n  remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration; playground RAG workflows (ingestion,\n  embedding, retrieval) run end-to-end against the provisioned store.\n- Deleting the playground configuration cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources\n  (garbage collection / finalization behaves correctly); pod restarts and credential\n  handling are resilient.\n- The database image is referenced through the operator's related-image mechanism so\n  disconnected installs resolve to the pinned digest.\n- The provisioned instance carries resource requests/limits derived from the\n  model-registry-operator reference values and the benchmark sizing recommendation.\n- The implementation demonstrably separates the provisioning point from the connection\n  consumption point (a shared platform connection string can be substituted for\n  self-provisioning without changing the consumer path).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n  provisioning: this epic is the delivery of that requirement under outcome A.\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store:\n  end-to-end acceptance criterion above.\n- **HLR-5 (P0)** — multi-tenant scoping: per-namespace isolation of the provisioned\n  instance.\n- **HLR-6 (P0)** — lightweight operation: benchmark-derived resource sizing applied.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Hard prerequisite: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator\n  modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) must be delivered; until then there is no\n  RHOAI-controlled operator where PostgreSQL lifecycle management can live.\n- Fallback if this outcome is not selected: BFF-managed provisioning (provisioning done\n  directly by the gen-ai BFF) or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56398,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b59d86a4638be6d4","agent_id":"a6f01f67c7f84a90b","session_id":"bb294bba-45da-456e-886f-d6e4ba682e14","uuid":"b19f879a-3a72-4aff-9939-efa1714a657d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:27:58.962Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
