{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b80ef2fa8d5a60f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector\n4\t  store (branch A)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard Crimson\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator\n18\t    modularization is not delivered in time for RHOAI 3.5, this epic is removed and\n19\t    provisioning falls back to BFF-managed provisioning or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 1\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 6\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store (branch A)\n37\t\n38\t> **Conditional branch epic — outcome A of the provisioning go/no-go decision.** Selected\n39\t> only if the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled\n40\t> operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5. If a different outcome is selected, this epic does\n41\t> not exist.\n42\t\n43\t## Description\n44\t\n45\tThis epic delivers the preferred provisioning outcome: PostgreSQL lifecycle management for\n46\tthe Gen AI Studio default vector store implemented in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\n47\tprovided by the dashboard operator modularization, following the model-registry-operator's\n48\testablished auto-provisioning pattern. When a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG capabilities\n49\tis configured, the operator provisions a dedicated PostgreSQL instance (with pgvector) in the\n50\tplayground's namespace, and the remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration consumes\n51\tthe provisioned connection string — giving users a default vector store that works\n52\tout-of-the-box with no manual setup.\n53\t\n54\tThe ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic;\n55\tthat is why the RHOAI-controlled operator layer is a hard prerequisite for this branch.\n56\t\n57\t## Scope\n58\t\n59\t- Implement PostgreSQL self-provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer following the\n60\t  model-registry-operator pattern: per-namespace Deployment, Service and credential Secret\n61\t  created when a playground with RAG is configured, consumed via a connection string.\n62\t- Use the existing Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector out of the\n63\t  box — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding work.\n64\t- Pin the database image for disconnected installs through the existing operator image\n65\t  reference mechanism (the PostgreSQL 16 related-image environment variable already present\n66\t  in the platform operator's CSV).\n67\t- Apply resource requests/limits to the provisioned PostgreSQL instance starting from the\n68\t  model-registry-operator's values, adjusted by the benchmark-derived sizing recommendation.\n69\t- Scope the instance per namespace (per-namespace isolation is the selected scoping model).\n70\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC\n71\t  becomes available (RHOAI 3.6+), the configuration consumes the shared connection string\n72\t  instead of self-provisioning.\n73\t\n74\t## Acceptance Criteria\n75\t\n76\t- Configuring a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG causes a PostgreSQL instance (pgvector\n77\t  included) to be provisioned in the playground's namespace, with no manual user setup\n78\t  steps.\n79\t- The provisioned instance's credentials are delivered via a Secret and consumed by the\n80\t  remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration; playground RAG workflows (ingestion,\n81\t  embedding, retrieval) run end-to-end against the provisioned store.\n82\t- Deleting the playground configuration cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources\n83\t  (garbage collection / finalization behaves correctly); pod restarts and credential\n84\t  handling are resilient.\n85\t- The database image is referenced through the operator's related-image mechanism so\n86\t  disconnected installs resolve to the pinned digest.\n87\t- The provisioned instance carries resource requests/limits derived from the\n88\t  model-registry-operator reference values and the benchmark sizing recommendation.\n89\t- The implementation demonstrably separates the provisioning point from the connection\n90\t  consumption point (a shared platform connection string can be substituted for\n91\t  self-provisioning without changing the consumer path).\n92\t\n93\t## HLR Traceability\n94\t\n95\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n96\t  provisioning: this epic is the delivery of that requirement under outcome A.\n97\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store:\n98\t  end-to-end acceptance criterion above.\n99\t- **HLR-5 (P0)** — multi-tenant scoping: per-namespace isolation of the provisioned\n100\t  instance.\n101\t- **HLR-6 (P0)** — lightweight operation: benchmark-derived resource sizing applied.\n102\t\n103\t## Notes\n104\t\n105\t- Hard prerequisite: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator\n106\t  modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) must be delivered; until then there is no\n107\t  RHOAI-controlled operator where PostgreSQL lifecycle management can live.\n108\t- Fallback if this outcome is not selected: BFF-managed provisioning (provisioning done\n109\t  directly by the gen-ai BFF) or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ea6f9b8cf5822b","agent_id":"a1ff60dd6c6038da7","session_id":"bb294bba-45da-456e-886f-d6e4ba682e14","uuid":"19e61421-192e-424d-a1f2-d4c4dd04e823","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:31:04.298Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b80ef2fa8d5a60f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
