{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7397aeabb2dc28a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 1\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004: Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio\n10\t\n11\t**Source basis:** The full strategy attachment (`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) referenced by the\n12\tstrategy body was not available in this workspace, so the Affected Components / Impacted Teams /\n13\tHLR / Dependencies / NFR tables could not be read (see Health Warnings). The decomposition is\n14\tderived from the strategy summary, its Acceptance Criteria, and the **Staff Engineer Input**,\n15\twhich takes precedence per the decomposition contract. All Staff Engineer overrides are logged\n16\tbelow.\n17\t\n18\t**Strategy in one line:** provide an out-of-the-box, pgvector-backed default vector store for\n19\tGen AI Studio playground RAG workflows so that removing the inline Milvus provider from the\n20\tOGX (Llama Stack) distribution (RHAISTRAT-7474) causes no functional regression — using the\n21\texisting Red Hat `postgresql-16` image (pgvector included, no custom image build, no Konflux\n22\tonboarding needed) and the largely-reusable existing remote vector store implementation.\n23\t\n24\t## Epic List\n25\t\n26\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n27\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Default vector store provisioning approach go/no-go for RHOAI 3.5 | Investigation | Dashboard Crimson | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio OGXServer instances | Implementation | Dashboard Crimson | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Capture inline Milvus baseline and benchmark pgvector for the default vector store | Implementation | Dashboard Crimson | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 | Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store (branch A) | Implementation | Dashboard Crimson | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store (branch B) | Implementation | Dashboard Crimson | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E004 | Bring-your-own PostgreSQL support for Gen AI Studio RAG (branch C) | Implementation | Dashboard Crimson | P1 |\n34\t\n35\t`epic_count` = 3 (main plan: E001–E003). The three `BRANCH-*-E004` files are conditional\n36\talternatives attached to the gating Investigation, not standalone main-plan nodes; exactly one\n37\tof them is selected by the E001 outcome.\n38\t\n39\t## Dependency DAG\n40\t\n41\tBranch epics are shown for context but are excluded from the main-plan critical path\n42\t(critical path length = 1: E001, E002 and E003 are mutually independent main-plan roots).\n43\t\n44\t```mermaid\n45\tgraph TD\n46\t    E001[\"E001 (Investigation): provisioning approach go/no-go\"]\n47\t    E002[\"E002: remote pgvector vector_io provider config\"]\n48\t    E003[\"E003: inline Milvus baseline + pgvector benchmark\"]\n49\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E004: operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning\"]\n50\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E004: BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning\"]\n51\t    BC[\"BRANCH-C-E004: bring-your-own PostgreSQL\"]\n52\t    E001 --> BA\n53\t    E001 --> BB\n54\t    E001 --> BC\n55\t    E002 --> BA\n56\t    E002 --> BB\n57\t    E002 --> BC\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t## DAG Justification\n61\t\n62\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n63\t|------|------|-----------|\n64\t| E001 → BRANCH-A/B/C-E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates existence) | The go/no-go decision on the PostgreSQL provisioning approach determines **which** provisioning epic exists at all: operator-based self-provisioning is only viable if the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands for 3.5; otherwise the fallback is BFF-managed provisioning or bring-your-own. All three branch epics carry `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-8004-E001` with `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` — each is a true gate (the epic may not exist under a different outcome). |\n65\t| E002 → BRANCH-A/B/C-E004 | Rule 12/13 (produced artifact consumed downstream) | The provisioning epics wire a database connection into the pgvector provider configuration surface that E002 builds (vector_io provider activation, connection-secret injection, decoupling from application storage). The branch code builds against that configuration capability, so it is serial after E002. |\n66\t| E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (independent, no shared artifact) | The remote pgvector provider configuration is identical in every outcome — the connection string differs only in who provisions the database. E002 is Tier 1 work and must not wait on the decision. |\n67\t| E003 ∥ E001, E003 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (independent) | The benchmark compares the current inline Milvus provider against a pgvector backend exercised through the existing remote vector store path; it does not need the BFF-driven configuration or the provisioning automation (a manually deployed pgvector instance suffices). It is Tier 1 risk-reduction work with a time-boxed window: the inline Milvus baseline must be captured **before** RHAISTRAT-7474 removes inline providers from the distribution image. |\n68\t| No repo-onboarding / license-validation / konflux-onboarding epics | Rules 19–21 (not applicable) | Staff Engineer Correction 2: the Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image already includes pgvector and is already referenced by the model-registry-operator and the rhods-operator CSV (`RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` for disconnected installs). No new component, no custom image, no onboarding chain. |\n69\t\n70\t## Staff Engineer Input Override Log\n71\t\n72\tThe Staff Engineer Input diverges from the AI-generated strategy in the following ways; the\n73\tStaff Engineer position was used throughout:\n74\t\n75\t1. **Auto Rag removed from scope.** The strategy's summary, acceptance criteria and validation\n76\t   requirements include Auto Rag; the Staff Engineer directs decoupling — Auto Rag integration\n77\t   with Gen AI Studio is RHAISTRAT-7824 (targeting RHOAI 3.6). This decomposition validates\n78\t   pgvector only for Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows.\n79\t2. **No custom image build / no Konflux onboarding.** The strategy's 1–2 sprint image\n80\t   onboarding estimate is eliminated (Correction 2): `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`\n81\t   ships pgvector; the model-registry-operator already auto-provisions it and\n82\t   `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` already exists in the rhods-operator CSV.\n83\t3. **Application storage is untouched.** Correction 3: OGX vector storage (`remote::pgvector`\n84\t   via `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) and application storage (`storage.kv.type` / `storage.sql.type`,\n85\t   default SQLite) are independent configurations. All SQLite→PostgreSQL migration and\n86\t   \"consolidate vector and application storage\" considerations from the strategy are removed.\n87\t4. **OGX does not auto-provision PostgreSQL.** Correction 1: introducing PostgreSQL for vector\n88\t   storage is new work, not an extension of existing infrastructure; the gen-ai BFF currently\n89\t   hardcodes SQLite when creating OGXServer instances.\n90\t5. **Platform-level shared database deferred.** A DSC-managed shared PostgreSQL is the\n91\t   long-term direction but will not exist until RHOAI 3.6; for 3.5 Gen AI Studio must\n92\t   provision its own instance (or require bring-your-own).\n93\t6. **Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 with fallbacks.** Self-provisioning following the\n94\t   model-registry-operator pattern requires a RHOAI-controlled operator (dashboard operator\n95\t   modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress). Modeled as the gating Investigation with\n96\t   three bounded outcomes (conditional branches), plus the Staff Engineer's second fallback\n97\t   (BFF-managed provisioning) as branch B.\n98\t7. **Performance thresholds removed.** No latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99), corpus-size ranges, or\n99\t   index-type selection: the default store targets development experimentation; the sprint 1\n100\t   benchmark only verifies pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus\n101\t   baseline, and flat scan (no index) is sufficient. PostgreSQL resource sizing starts from\n102\t   the model-registry-operator's requests/limits.\n103\t\n104\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n105\t\n106\tThe numbered HLR section resides in the unavailable strategy attachment. HLRs below are\n107\tderived one-to-one from the strategy's Acceptance Criteria (in order); HLR-3 is dropped per\n108\tStaff Engineer override 1. Priorities inherit the strategy frontmatter priority (`Blocker`\n109\t→ P0).\n110\t\n111\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n112\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n113\t| HLR-1 — default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning/configuration | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004, RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | Fully satisfied only by the self-provisioning branches. Branch C is the explicit degraded fallback (bring-your-own) and does not satisfy this HLR — accepted by the Staff Engineer as aligned with OGX 1.0 breaking changes. |\n114\t| HLR-2 — Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 (provider wiring), BRANCH-A/B/C-E004 (end-to-end out-of-the-box path), RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 (verification) | E002 delivers the provider configuration; each branch epic carries the end-to-end playground RAG acceptance criterion; E003 measures \"no loss of capability\". |\n115\t| HLR-3 — Auto Rag functions with the default vector store | — | **Removed from scope** | Staff Engineer override 1: decoupled to RHAISTRAT-7824 (RHOAI 3.6). No orphaned work — no epic covers Auto Rag by design. |\n116\t| HLR-4 — default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack / OGX instance | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | The remote `remote::pgvector` vector_io provider configuration is exactly this decoupling: PostgreSQL runs outside the OGX process, and application storage remains on its existing SQLite default (Correction 3). |\n117\t| HLR-5 — scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004, RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | Per-namespace scoping is the Staff Engineer's preferred model (the per-instance alternative existed only for Auto Rag, now out of scope) and is an acceptance criterion on both self-provisioning branches. |\n118\t| HLR-6 — lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 (sizing), BRANCH-A/B-E004 (resource requests/limits) | E003 produces the sizing recommendation (model-registry-operator values as starting point, adjusted per benchmark); the self-provisioning branches apply it. |\n119\t\n120\tOpen questions from the strategy, resolved by the Staff Engineer Input (logged, not\n121\tInvestigations): the scoping model (per-namespace, since Auto Rag is decoupled) and the\n122\tmigration path to a production-grade vector database (portability acceptance criterion on the\n123\tself-provisioning branches: consume a shared platform connection string once RHOAI 3.6\n124\tprovides one, rather than self-provisioning).\n125\t\n126\t## Health Warnings\n127\t\n128\t1. **Missing strategy attachment (health warning per Step 1).** The full strategy\n129\t   (`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md` attachment) was not provisioned in this workspace, so the\n130\t   Affected Components, Impacted Teams, HLR, Dependencies and NFR tables could not be parsed.\n131\t   HLRs were derived from the Acceptance Criteria; **teams were inferred** — all epics are\n132\t   assigned to \"Dashboard Crimson\" based on the strategy's `dashboard-crimson-scrum` label and\n133\t   the Staff Engineer's description of the Gen AI Studio development team owning the go/no-go\n134\t   decision. Verify team assignments against Jira before scheduling.\n135\t2. **External timing risk — RHAISTRAT-7164.** The dashboard operator modularization is a hard\n136\t   dependency for the preferred (operator-based) provisioning approach and is still In\n137\t   Progress; the Staff Engineer notes it will be challenging to commit this strategy to a\n138\t   specific release until it lands. Mitigated by the E001 go/no-go Investigation and three\n139\t   conditional branches, but the schedule risk itself is outside this strategy's control.\n140\t3. **Architecture-context gaps.** Several load-bearing specifics are asserted by the Staff\n141\t   Engineer Input but not corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/`: the\n142\t   `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` activation variable and `llamastack_config.go` SQLite hardcoding (no\n143\t   OGXServer spec schema or env-var inventory in `ogx-k8s-operator.md` /\n144\t   `ogx-distribution.md`), the guardrails-infrastructure provisioning precedent in the gen-ai\n145\t   BFF (`odh-dashboard.md` documents NeMo Guardrails only as an egress destination), the\n146\t   `postgresql-16` image name / `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` (no RELATED_IMAGE vars in\n147\t   `model-registry-operator.md` or `rhods-operator.md`), and the model-registry PostgreSQL\n148\t   resource requests/limits. What the context files **do** corroborate: PGVector is a shipped\n149\t   remote vector I/O backend in the OGX distribution and the inline providers (including\n150\t   milvus-inline) are stripped from the build; the ogx-k8s-operator reconciles only the OGX\n151\t   server workload (no database provisioning); the model-registry-operator does auto-provision\n152\t   per-CR PostgreSQL Deployments/Services/credential Secrets. The uncorroborated items are\n153\t   implementation details to confirm at epic start, not structural unknowns.\n154\t4. **Priority note (not an inversion).** E003 (benchmark) is P0 despite blocking nothing: the\n155\t   inline Milvus baseline is only measurable before RHAISTRAT-7474 removes the inline\n156\t   providers — a closing window makes it sprint-1-critical — and it is the measurement\n157\t   instrument for the P0 \"no loss of current capability\" criterion.\n158\t5. **Scope trap avoided — branch C does not satisfy HLR-1.** The bring-your-own fallback\n159\t   ships a degraded out-of-the-box experience by design (manual user setup). This is an\n160\t   accepted product trade-off per the Staff Engineer, recorded here so the review does not\n161\t   read it as an coverage gap. Branch C is P1: it is the minimal residual path, deferrable\n162\t   documentation-heavy work relative to the P0 self-provisioning branches.\n163\t\n164\t## Tiered Delivery\n165\t\n166\t- **Tier 1 (independent of RHAISTRAT-7164 timing, start immediately):**\n167\t  - **E002** — remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration (identical in every\n168\t    outcome; the existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable, so this is\n169\t    the small part of the effort).\n170\t  - **E003** — inline Milvus baseline capture plus pgvector benchmark and sizing\n171\t    recommendation (risk-reduction validation with a closing measurement window).\n172\t- **Tier 2 (gated by the E001 decision on the RHAISTRAT-7164 hard dependency):**\n173\t  - **BRANCH-A-E004** (operator-based self-provisioning, preferred), **BRANCH-B-E004**\n174\t    (BFF-managed provisioning, fallback), **BRANCH-C-E004** (bring-your-own, residual\n175\t    fallback). Exactly one branch is executed.\n176\t\n177\t## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n178\t\n179\tThe E001 Investigation has three bounded outcomes; one branch epic file exists per outcome:\n180\t\n181\t| Outcome | Condition | Branch file |\n182\t|---------|-----------|-------------|\n183\t| A | RHAISTRAT-7164 operator layer lands in time for RHOAI 3.5 | `RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md` |\n184\t| B | RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land; BFF-managed provisioning fallback chosen | `RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004.md` |\n185\t| C | Neither self-provisioning path lands; customers bring their own PostgreSQL | `RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E004.md` |\n186\t\n187\tAll branch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-8004-E001` (also in `dependencies`, together\n188\twith `RHAISTRAT-8004-E002`) and `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` — under a different\n189\toutcome the epic does not exist. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its dependencies.\n190\t\n191\t## Component Mapping Notes\n192\t\n193\t- **Gen AI Studio** (canonical) is used for all playground/gen-ai-BFF-scoped epics (E001,\n194\t  E002, E003, branches B and C): the work lives in the odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF\n195\t  (`packages/gen-ai/`) and its OGXServer-instance creation path, in service of the Gen AI\n196\t  Studio playground.\n197\t- **AI Core Dashboard** (canonical) is used for branch A only: operator-based provisioning\n198\t  lives in the dashboard operator layer delivered by the RHAISTRAT-7164 modularization — the\n199\t  odh-dashboard/dashboard-operator surface rather than the gen-ai package. This is the single\n200\t  most-relevant canonical name for that span; the strategy itself named no components\n201\t  (attachment missing).\n202\t- **No OGX-side epic.** The OGX distribution already ships the PGVector remote vector I/O\n203\t  provider and already strips the inline providers — no `OGX Core` / `LlamaStack` changes are\n204\t  in scope; all work is configuration and provisioning on the RHOAI side.\n205\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b84cb063040b3231","agent_id":"abbe6fcfcdce2072c","session_id":"bb294bba-45da-456e-886f-d6e4ba682e14","uuid":"c04ea60d-1d93-487e-a412-75a599b221eb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:34:17.745Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7397aeabb2dc28a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
