{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0dd38c42d7cab85","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio OGXServer\n4\t  instances\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Dashboard Crimson\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio OGXServer instances\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers the vector-store-side wiring that is common to **every** provisioning\n35\toutcome: configuring the OGX instances created for the Gen AI Studio playground to use the\n36\tremote pgvector vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`)\n37\tinstead of the removed inline Milvus provider. The existing remote vector store\n38\timplementation is largely reusable — per the engineering team, the provider integration is\n39\tthe small part of this strategy's effort — so this epic is configuration and wiring work in\n40\tthe gen-ai BFF's OGXServer-instance creation path, not new provider development in the OGX\n41\tdistribution.\n42\t\n43\tThis work is deliberately decoupled from, and runs in parallel with, the provisioning\n44\tapproach decision: whichever outcome is selected (operator-based self-provisioning,\n45\tBFF-managed provisioning, or bring-your-own PostgreSQL), the OGX vector I/O configuration is\n46\tthe same — only the source of the PostgreSQL connection string differs.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider on OGXServer instances created for the Gen\n51\t  AI Studio playground (activation via the `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment guard, following the\n52\t  distribution's conditional provider-activation pattern).\n53\t- Inject the PostgreSQL connection details (host, port, database, credentials) through the\n54\t  existing secret-resolution mechanism (Secret-backed environment variables), so the same\n55\t  wiring works whether the database is provisioned by the operator layer, by the BFF, or\n56\t  supplied by the user.\n57\t- Keep OGX **application storage** untouched: `storage.kv.type` and `storage.sql.type` remain\n58\t  on their existing SQLite default. Vector storage and application storage are independent\n59\t  configurations; there is no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration concern in this epic.\n60\t- Preserve the escape hatch: the vector store configuration can be pointed at an external,\n61\t  user-managed vector database instead of the default pgvector instance (users with\n62\t  production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external database).\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- An OGXServer instance created for a Gen AI Studio playground activates the remote\n67\t  pgvector vector_io provider, and the provider connects successfully to a PostgreSQL\n68\t  instance with pgvector available when its connection details are supplied.\n69\t- Connection credentials are read from a Kubernetes Secret via the distribution's\n70\t  secret-resolution mechanism — no database credentials appear in plaintext in the\n71\t  OGXServer spec, ConfigMap or logs.\n72\t- The OGX application storage backend remains on its existing default (SQLite) — verified\n73\t  unchanged by this configuration work.\n74\t- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows (document ingestion, embedding, retrieval) complete\n75\t  successfully against a pgvector-backed vector store with no loss of the current inline\n76\t  Milvus capability, when a reachable pgvector endpoint is supplied.\n77\t- Pointing the configuration at an external vector database (connection details swapped)\n78\t  is demonstrated to work — the default is an opinionated default, not a lock-in.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector\n83\t  store with no loss of current capability: this epic is the provider wiring that makes the\n84\t  playground talk to pgvector.\n85\t- **HLR-4 (P0)** — the default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the\n86\t  OGX instance: the remote `remote::pgvector` provider configuration is exactly this\n87\t  decoupling; no inline provider is used.\n88\t\n89\t## Notes\n90\t\n91\t- Strategy open questions on latency thresholds, corpus size and index type are resolved by\n92\t  the Staff Engineer Input as out of scope: the default store targets development\n93\t  experimentation, flat scan (no index) is sufficient, and performance is verified by the\n94\t  benchmark workstream (order-of-magnitude parity with the inline Milvus baseline), not by\n95\t  SLAs.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b241ea264dcfc8af","agent_id":"af08417c6040f36f6","session_id":"bb294bba-45da-456e-886f-d6e4ba682e14","uuid":"beb6a9ef-d609-4be6-b0c8-c8a13c56eecc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:36:27.369Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0dd38c42d7cab85","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
