{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6c44e55748bcf71","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector\n4\t  store (branch A)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard Crimson\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: remove\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator\n19\t    modularization is not delivered in time for RHOAI 3.5, this epic is removed and\n20\t    provisioning falls back to BFF-managed provisioning or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 1\n27\t  external_dependency: -1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 6\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store (branch A)\n38\t\n39\t> **Conditional branch epic — outcome A of the provisioning go/no-go decision.** Selected\n40\t> only if the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled\n41\t> operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5. If a different outcome is selected, this epic does\n42\t> not exist.\n43\t\n44\t## Description\n45\t\n46\tThis epic delivers the preferred provisioning outcome: PostgreSQL lifecycle management for\n47\tthe Gen AI Studio default vector store implemented in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\n48\tprovided by the dashboard operator modularization, following the model-registry-operator's\n49\testablished auto-provisioning pattern. When a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG capabilities\n50\tis configured, the operator provisions a dedicated PostgreSQL instance (with pgvector) in the\n51\tplayground's namespace, and the remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration consumes\n52\tthe provisioned connection string — giving users a default vector store that works\n53\tout-of-the-box with no manual setup.\n54\t\n55\tThe ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic;\n56\tthat is why the RHOAI-controlled operator layer is a hard prerequisite for this branch.\n57\t\n58\t## Scope\n59\t\n60\t- Implement PostgreSQL self-provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer following the\n61\t  model-registry-operator pattern: per-namespace Deployment, Service and credential Secret\n62\t  created when a playground with RAG is configured, consumed via a connection string.\n63\t- Use the existing Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector out of the\n64\t  box — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding work.\n65\t- Pin the database image for disconnected installs through the existing operator image\n66\t  reference mechanism (the PostgreSQL 16 related-image environment variable already present\n67\t  in the platform operator's CSV).\n68\t- Apply resource requests/limits to the provisioned PostgreSQL instance starting from the\n69\t  model-registry-operator's values, adjusted by the benchmark-derived sizing recommendation.\n70\t- Scope the instance per namespace (per-namespace isolation is the selected scoping model).\n71\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC\n72\t  becomes available (RHOAI 3.6+), the configuration consumes the shared connection string\n73\t  instead of self-provisioning.\n74\t\n75\t## Acceptance Criteria\n76\t\n77\t- Configuring a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG causes a PostgreSQL instance (pgvector\n78\t  included) to be provisioned in the playground's namespace, with no manual user setup\n79\t  steps.\n80\t- The provisioned instance's credentials are delivered via a Secret and consumed by the\n81\t  remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration; playground RAG workflows (ingestion,\n82\t  embedding, retrieval) run end-to-end against the provisioned store.\n83\t- Deleting the playground configuration cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources\n84\t  (garbage collection / finalization behaves correctly); pod restarts and credential\n85\t  handling are resilient.\n86\t- The database image is referenced through the operator's related-image mechanism so\n87\t  disconnected installs resolve to the pinned digest.\n88\t- The provisioned instance carries resource requests/limits derived from the\n89\t  model-registry-operator reference values and the benchmark sizing recommendation.\n90\t- The implementation demonstrably separates the provisioning point from the connection\n91\t  consumption point (a shared platform connection string can be substituted for\n92\t  self-provisioning without changing the consumer path).\n93\t\n94\t## HLR Traceability\n95\t\n96\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n97\t  provisioning: this epic is the delivery of that requirement under outcome A.\n98\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store:\n99\t  end-to-end acceptance criterion above.\n100\t- **HLR-5 (P0)** — multi-tenant scoping: per-namespace isolation of the provisioned\n101\t  instance.\n102\t- **HLR-6 (P0)** — lightweight operation: benchmark-derived resource sizing applied.\n103\t\n104\t## Notes\n105\t\n106\t- Hard prerequisite: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator\n107\t  modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) must be delivered; until then there is no\n108\t  RHOAI-controlled operator where PostgreSQL lifecycle management can live.\n109\t- Fallback if this outcome is not selected: BFF-managed provisioning (provisioning done\n110\t  directly by the gen-ai BFF) or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b241ea264dcfc8af","agent_id":"af08417c6040f36f6","session_id":"bb294bba-45da-456e-886f-d6e4ba682e14","uuid":"7610a50a-a213-4708-b067-5429a0e56324","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:36:31.180Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6c44e55748bcf71","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
